NJ"},"stage":"passed_origin","stage_label":"Passed one chamber","summary":"The Faster Labor Contracts Act sets strict timelines and procedures for employers and newly recognized labor unions to finalize their first collective bargaining agreement. If parties cannot reach an agreement through direct negotiations and mediation, the dispute is sent to a binding arbitration panel.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Must begin negotiations within 10 days of a written request, maintain existing employment terms during talks, continue bargaining obligations unless decertified, and abide by a binding two-year contract if forced into arbitration.","group":"Employers"},{"effect":"Gain structured deadlines for negotiating a first contract, access to federal mediation after 90 days, and access to binding arbitration if mediation fails to produce a contract within 30 days.","group":"Employees and Labor Organizations"}],"key_provisions":["Employers and newly recognized or certified labor representatives must begin bargaining within 10 days of receiving a written request.","If no agreement is reached after 90 days of bargaining, either party may request mediation from the Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service (FMCS).","If mediation fails after 30 days, the FMCS refers the dispute to a three-person arbitration panel to render a binding decision.","Arbitration panels must base their decisions on factors including the employer's financial status, operations size, employee cost of living, employee financial sustainability, and wages paid by other employers in the same business.","The resulting arbitration decision creates a collective bargaining agreement that binds both parties for two years, unless they mutually agree to amend it.","Employers must maintain current wages, hours, and employment conditions during negotiations, and their duty to bargain continues unless the representative is officially decertified.","The Government Accountability Office (GAO) must report to Congress within one year on the average number of days it takes to reach an initial contract after representative certification or recognition."],"missing_information":["Details on how arbitration panel members are compensated or who pays for their expenses.","Specific penalties or enforcement mechanisms if an employer or union fails to meet the 10-day meeting requirement or refuses to participate in arbitration."],"plain_summary":"The Faster Labor Contracts Act sets strict timelines and procedures for employers and newly recognized labor unions to finalize their first collective bargaining agreement. If parties cannot reach an agreement through direct negotiations and mediation, the dispute is sent to a binding arbitration panel.","significance":"This bill establishes federal intervention mechanisms for initial workplace labor contracts, shifting from purely voluntary negotiations to mandatory mediation and binding arbitration after specific timeframes."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-27T12:49:49+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5408/BILLS-119hr5408eh.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Faster Labor Contracts Act","viability":73.3,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Passed one chamber"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":28.0,"value":0.8,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Floor activity","value":"Passed a chamber"}],"key":"floor","label":"Floor consideration","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"ef